From f736e9831bf97e0ce6dc68bada33917e0eeed603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:41:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] launcher support: UTF-8 command line on Windows, Windows
 handoff without a second engine, digest-cache temp files

- main.cpp: decode the wide command line to UTF-8 on Windows (the CRT argv
  is ANSI and loses non-ASCII characters in user names / data folders);
  warn about unknown options instead of ignoring them silently.
- ps2_runtime.cpp loadExecPS2: handoff file is read through the wide
  environment on Windows and written as UTF-8; without the launcher a
  Windows handoff is refused with a message (the old _execv spawned a second
  engine and returned into the first, leaving two engines on one memory
  card). Linux exec path unchanged.
- ps2_disc_mount.cpp: the digest cache is written through a per-process
  temporary that is removed on failure (the launcher writes the same file),
  LOCALAPPDATA is read as wide, the cache hit or miss is logged, and the
  cache is documented as a convenience, not a security boundary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_disc_mount.cpp | 48 ++++++++++++++--
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp    | 76 ++++++++++++--------------
 ps2xRuntime/src/main.cpp               | 42 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

